# Encore Bridge settings for Docker. Every setting here is optional: the setup guide on the admin page
# (http://<this computer's address>:8095/admin) asks for what the bridge needs. To set something here anyway, copy
# this file to .env next to compose.yaml, fill it in, then start (or restart) the bridge with: docker compose up -d
# Keep .env private.

# Your own Spotify developer app's Client ID (no client secret is needed). Optional. The setup guide on the admin page
# saves it for you (in data/settings.json). A value here wins over the guide's, and the guide can't change it.
# The app, if you make it by hand (the setup guide shows the same steps):
#   1. Sign in at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard and create an app (any name and description).
#      Pick "Web API", and add this exact Redirect URI: http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback
#   2. In the app's User Management, add the Spotify account you use with Encore (Spotify Premium).
#   3. Paste the app's Client ID here.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# The admin page's password (any user name works). Leave it empty: the setup guide asks for one when you first open
# http://<this computer's address>:8095/admin, together with the setup code shown by:
#   docker compose logs gateway | grep "setup code"
# A password set here always wins over one chosen on the admin page.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Who may open the admin page and pair a phone: addresses or CIDR ranges, separated by commas. Empty means "private":
# this computer, the private home-network ranges and 100.64.0.0/10 (VPN overlays such as Tailscale).
# Pair at home: the pairing reply carries the phone's key.
#ADMIN_ALLOW=private

# Encore Bridge looks for a new version on GitHub once a day. It sends only its version number; GitHub sees this
# computer's public IP address, as with any download. Set this to 0 to turn the daily check off ("Check now" in the
# admin page's Updates section still works when you choose it).
#UPDATE_CHECK=1
